From e7b98c1bb2e3fe7c1696c7b1bdd54cd5ff52c3bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:36:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] VAX8200: DMB32 sync line, CTS follows RTS (DDCMP tributary)

The DMB32 synchronous line reported its modem inputs as constant while
connected: clocks, CTS, DCD and DSR all on.  VMS V5.5's SIDRIVER as a
DDCMP multipoint tributary (DECnet line DMB-0 PROTOCOL DDCMP TRIBUTARY)
drives an RTS/CTS handshake: to transmit it raises RTS and waits for CTS,
after the message it drops RTS and waits for CTS to drop before it is
idle again.  With CTS stuck on, SIDRIVER hung in the "wait for CTS off"
state after its first transmission, never sent DECnet's reply and
restarted the line: the circuit stayed "on -starting" against a DMP11
control station.

Now, while the line is up (connected or looped), CTS follows RTS
(LPR2 bit 4), as with a modem or a null-modem cable; a write of LPR2
updates the inputs at once and a CTS change is a modem status entry in
SBUF (unless LPR1 MODEM.SUPPRESS).  Point-to-point operation keeps RTS on
and is unchanged.

Tests: VAX 8200 VMS V5.5 tributary 4 against a VAX-11/780 VMS V4.7 DMP11
control station: circuit up, NCP LOOP NODE 20 x 500, DIRECTORY and COPY;
DMB32 point-to-point against a MicroVAX II DMV11 (tests/dmb32/p4.sh): PASS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SuavtftJEqWTX7fajw6zWU
---
 VAX/vax_dmb.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/VAX/vax_dmb.c b/VAX/vax_dmb.c
index 01b79d3a..e55e0def 100644
--- a/VAX/vax_dmb.c
+++ b/VAX/vax_dmb.c
@@ -289,6 +289,7 @@
 
 /* sync LPR2 (3.3.35) */
 #define L2_OUTPUTS      0x0000001F              /* modem control outputs */
+#define  L2_RTS          0x00000010             /* request to send */
 #define L2_V_INPUTS     8
 #define L2_INPUTS       0x0000FF00              /* modem status inputs (ro) */
 #define  SM_RXCLK        0x0100                 /* receive clock running */
@@ -1224,11 +1225,15 @@ dmb_sreg[SY_BUFCTRL] = BC_CABLE;
 dmb_sl.frame_len = 0;
 }
 
-/* The modem inputs: all on while connected to the peer or looped. */
+/* The modem inputs: on while connected to the peer or looped, CTS only
+   while RTS is on (as from a modem, or a null-modem cable that loops RTS to
+   CTS).  VMS V5.5's SIDRIVER as a DDCMP multipoint tributary raises RTS to
+   transmit, waits for CTS, and after the message drops RTS and waits for CTS
+   to drop before it may transmit again (known issues 84). */
 static uint32 dmb_sync_inputs (void)
 {
 if (combo_sync_up (&dmb_sl) || (dmb_sreg[SY_LPR1] & L1_LOOP))
-    return SM_UP;
+    return (SM_UP & ~SM_CTS) | ((dmb_sreg[SY_LPR2] & L2_RTS) ? SM_CTS : 0);
 return 0;
 }
 
@@ -1432,6 +1437,7 @@ switch (idx) {
         break;
     case SY_LPR2:                               /* modem inputs are read only */
         dmb_sreg[idx] = (data & ~L2_INPUTS) | (dmb_sreg[idx] & L2_INPUTS);
+        dmb_sync_modem ();                      /* CTS follows RTS */
         dmb_sync_kick ();
         break;
     case SY_BUFCTRL:                            /* cable fields are read only */
